### MiniLedger REST API Client Collection
@baseUrl = http://localhost:4000
@authToken = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1. Health Check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
Accept: application/json

### 2. Request OTP (Generates 6-digit OTP, logged to backend console)
# @name requestOtp
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/request-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+919876543210"
}

### 3. Verify OTP (Creates user on first login, returns JWT accessToken)
# Replace "123456" with the OTP printed in the backend server log
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/verify-otp
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+919876543210",
  "otp": "123456"
}

### 4. Get Current User Profile (Protected)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 5. Create a New Loan Entry
# @name createLoan
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "friendName": "Rohan Sharma",
  "amount": 2500.50,
  "dueDate": "2026-11-15"
}

### 6. Get Loans (Sorted Overdue First, then DueDate Asc)
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans?page=1&limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 7. Filter Loans by Status (PENDING)
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans?status=PENDING
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 8. Filter Overdue Loans Only
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans?overdue=true
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 9. Get Single Loan by ID
@loanId = {{createLoan.response.body.loan.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 10. Mark Loan as Repaid (Idempotent, conditional update)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/repay
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 11. Test Double Repay (Should return 409 Conflict)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/repay
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 12. Get Aggregated Financial Summary (Single aggregate SQL query)
GET {{baseUrl}}/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 13. Upload Loan Receipt Image (Multipart Form-Data)
# Requires a valid JPEG, PNG, or WebP file
POST {{baseUrl}}/loans/{{loanId}}/receipt
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="receipt"; filename="receipt.jpg"
Content-Type: image/jpeg

< ./uploads/sample.jpg
------WebKitFormBoundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--
